  "notes": "{果|は}たす means to fulfill, accomplish, or carry out something to completion. A somewhat formal verb used for duties, promises, and goals.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: 〜を{果|は}たす\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {役割|やくわり}を{果|は}たす: to fulfill a role\n- {約束|やくそく}を{果|は}たす: to keep a promise\n- {責任|せきにん}を{果|は}たす: to fulfill one's responsibility\n- {義務|ぎむ}を{果|は}たす: to carry out one's duty\n- {目的|もくてき}を{果|は}たす: to achieve one's purpose\n- {夢|ゆめ}を{果|は}たす: to realize one's dream\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {果|は}たして: as expected; indeed; really (adverb — different usage)\n- {果|は}てる: to end, to be exhausted (intransitive)\n\nREGISTER:\nSlightly formal. Often used in written language, speeches, and news. In casual speech, する or やる may replace it.",
